# Analysis was done using SNeP1.1 software
# Barbato, M., Orozco-terWengel, P., Tapio, M., & Bruford, M. W. (2015). SNeP: a tool to estimate trends in recent effective population size trajectories 
using genome-wide SNP data. Front Genet. 2015; 6: 109.

# for all chromosomes
~/SNeP1.1 -maf 0.01 -maxsnp 1000000 -ped file.ped -map file.map -ld -svedf

or

# program already install in the server and can be recall with just the software name i.e., SNeP
SNeP -maf 0.01 -maxsnp 1000000 -ped file.ped -map file.map -ld -svedf


# for particulare chr6 only, with maf equals to 0 (no minor allele frequency filtering)
~/SNeP1.1 -maf 0 -maxsnp 1000000 -chr 6 -ped file.ped -map file.map -ld -svedf

# Notes
Never use chromosome 0, as it may cause SNeP to go on loop
Need chromosomes named in numbers 1,2,3....29 and not contig names


